<h1>Build call screening with VoiceML.</h1>
<p class="lede">The McCallisters are a fictional family with a house phone to protect. Known nuisance numbers are refused before the call is answered, family numbers ring straight through, and every other caller says their name and why they&rsquo;re calling, which speech recognition checks before anyone is disturbed. It runs on three documents published on voiceml.org, with no application server.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ site.voicemlReferenceUrl }}/verbs/gather/">&lt;Gather&gt; reference</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What callers get</h2>
	<ul class="features-grid">
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "shield-check" %}</span>
			<h3>A block list</h3>
			<p>Numbers on the block list hear a busy signal. <code>&lt;Reject&gt;</code> refuses the call before it is answered, so it isn&rsquo;t charged.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "person-vcard" %}</span>
			<h3>A family list</h3>
			<p>Calls from family numbers ring the house without any questions.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "chat-text" %}</span>
			<h3>Spoken screening</h3>
			<p>Everyone else says their name and the reason for the call. Speech recognition turns it into text, and the next document decides what to do with it.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "telephone" %}</span>
			<h3>Rules on what was said</h3>
			<p>Family calling from an unknown number and the pizza delivery are put through. The Wet Bandits are refused by name, whatever number they use.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "record-circle" %}</span>
			<h3>Voicemail for the rest</h3>
			<p>Callers who match no rule leave a message instead of ringing the house.</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

